msgid "PWM 8-10 in group4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405wing.rst:119
#: 8afb235c71cf4be49ad87cbbd73d1de1
msgid "PWM 11,12 in group5  Note: PWM12 is setup for serial LED use by default, if PWM11 is used for motors or servos, you must re-assign PMW12 to a normal PWM output or nothing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405wing.rst:122
#: 8bd53f5afe714d0bbfd22ffdfcf34bad
msgid "RC Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405wing.rst:124
#: b37538415a8a4e67a3b5fdacf4d4584f
msgid "The SBUS pin, is passed by an inverter to RX2 (UART2 RX), which by default is mapped to a timer input instead of the UART, and can be used for all ArduPilot supported receiver protocols, except CRSF/ELRS and SRXL2 which require a true UART connection. However, FPort, when connected in this manner, can provide RC without telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405wing.rst:126
#: bb84012a81bc45bb9411e58d1dddfae7
msgid "To allow CRSF and embedded telemetry available in Fport, CRSF, and SRXL2 receivers, the UART1 should be used. With this option, :ref:`SERIAL11_PROTOCOL<SERIAL1_PROTOCOL>` must be set to \"23\" (already set by default), and:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405wing.rst:128
#: 9385f3be8999413eb0ad59e6b42435f2
msgid "PPM is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405wing.rst:130
#: 6929fb03b85e477cb18dc1a9755af191
msgid "DSM/SRXL connects to the RX1  pin, but SBUS would still be connected to SBUS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405wing.rst:132
#: fa7da7f658414dd1af651e9899b035c7
msgid "FPort requires connection to TX1 and RX1 via a bi-directional inverter. See :ref:`common-FPort-receivers`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405wing.rst:134
#: 7a7a9be99f7a4bc2b7447b66a89e1a9c
msgid "CRSF also requires a TX1 connection, in addition to RX1 and automatically provides telemetry. ELRS is connected in the same way, but bit 13 of :ref:`RC_OPTIONS<RC_OPTIONS>` should be set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405wing.rst:136
#: b0b80ed215ed46659245e1f1ef06e3cb
msgid "SRXL2 requires a connection to TX1 and automatically provides telemetry.  Set :ref:`SERIAL1_OPTIONS<SERIAL1_OPTIONS>` to \"4\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405wing.rst:138
#: 90dd432225ec4682b31b1aacbc1f067d
msgid "UART1 is configured by default for serial receivers. You can also have more than one receiver in the system at a time (usually used for long range hand-offs to a remote TX). See :ref:`common-multiple-rx` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405wing.rst:140
#: 57cf882a0d3446a1aa8410a4ca419931
msgid "Any UART can be used for RC system connections in ArduPilot also, and is compatible with all protocols except PPM (SBUS requires external inversion on other UARTs). See :ref:`common-rc-systems` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405wing.rst:142
#: b65ff4cd2d504d3faa80c77ba3b65455
msgid "the \"4V5\" pin above the SBUS pin and the 4V5 pins in the GPS, Airspeed, and Telem connectors are powered when USB is connected. Be careful not to present too much load to the USB source or voltage droop may occur. All other 5V pins are only powered when battery is present."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405wing.rst:145
#: fdf39599825e47cbba9ee50668b3322a
msgid "WIFI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405wing.rst:147
#: 338ccd76a745479997b9ad6d2db0002e
msgid "The SpeedyBeeF405Wing has an integrated wireless module allowing connections to GCS via WIFI. See the user manual for instructions. While BT is advertised as an alternate mode, this has not been proven to work with all BT dongles or cell-phones by ArduPilot. The WIFI mode has been tested with a variety of systems, however. Be sure the :ref:`SERIAL6_BAUD<SERIAL6_BAUD>` = 115 and that nothing is loading the TX6/RX6 pins which are connected to the wireless module, by default.."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405wing.rst:150
#: 0b818b457335411b9a666b41b15f942b
msgid "OSD Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-speedybeef405wing.rst:152
#: d2d3d302183746778d72e6aa156512ea
msgid "The SpeedyBeeF405Wing supports using its internal OSD using OSD_TYPE 1 (MAX7456 driver). External OSD support such as DJI or DisplayPort is supported using UART5 or any other free UART. See :ref:`common-msp-osd-overview-4.2` for more info."
msgstr ""

